herdr-music — third-party license notices
=========================================

shairplay (https://github.com/metaneutrons/shairplay-rust)
License: LGPL-3.0-or-later

Used to implement the AirPlay 1 (RAOP) receiver behind the `airplay`
provider. Rust links crate dependencies statically, so shairplay object
code is combined into the Apache-2.0 herdr-music binary.

LGPL-3.0 §4(d)(0) permits this combination when the user can relink
against a modified library. herdr-music satisfies that by construction:
the plugin is distributed as source and `herdr plugin install`/`link`
runs `cargo build --release` on the user's machine — replacing the
crate version in Cargo.toml and rebuilding *is* the relink.

A copy of the LGPL-3.0 ships with the shairplay crate source; cargo
vendors it under ~/.cargo/registry when building.
